The key takeaway is that type narrowing in nested scopes isn't automatically inherited. By using an assertion, assigning to a temporary variable, or passing the variable explicitly, you can help the type checker understand the correct type in the inner scope. The assertion method is often the most straightforward and least intrusive solution. 🚀

